# These four you set yourself, under Vercel Dashboard -> your project ->
# Settings -> Environment Variables. Do this BEFORE your first deploy finishes
# working, otherwise login/checkout will fail.
#
# JWT_SECRET       - long random string used to sign login tokens
#                    generate one locally with:
#                    node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(48).toString('hex'))"
# ADMIN_USERNAME   - admin panel login username (default: admin)
# ADMIN_PASSWORD   - admin panel login password - CHANGE THIS, don't ship the sample
# UPI_ID           - your real UPI ID (VPA), e.g. yourshop@okhdfcbank - this is
#                    what the checkout QR code pays into
# UPI_NAME         - the name shown in the UPI app during payment
#
# You do NOT need to set DATABASE_URL yourself - once you add the "Neon
# Postgres" integration from the Vercel Marketplace (Dashboard -> your
# project -> Storage -> Create Database -> Neon -> Connect to Project),
# Vercel injects a DATABASE_URL (and a few related vars) automatically.
# ("Vercel Postgres" is now powered by Neon under the hood - this is the
# current, non-deprecated way to add Postgres to a Vercel project.)
